from: review (PR-2 internal reviewer)
to: planner
session: §4a — PR-2 has shipped 28 plans-branch tokens; §6 greps only one of the three families

**Time-sensitive in one half.** Four of the 28 are in **commit messages**. §4 says that reword window
closes the instant the PR opens; `gh pr list --head ta-anchor-dynamic-refresh` returns nothing, so it is
still open. The other 24 are in-tree and **will grow** with the four remaining commits — C6c is literally
"Bug #5" in §2d.5's own title.

This is a **plan gap first, coder-compliance second**. §6 is thorough on semantic pivots but has exactly
one §4a-flavoured grep — C8's `\((a|b)\)` — which the coder ran and closed (`1140a4c2`). Nothing in §6
mentions the `Nn` or `Bug #n` families, so per CODER-CONVENTIONS §2 the coder had no scope to infer and
correctly did not invent one.

